---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The PDF at /dean-phillips-resume.pdf is printed from this page by scripts/resume-pdf.mjs,
// so edit the resume here and rerun the script. The print styles at the bottom are the PDF's look.
const pdf = '/dean-phillips-resume.pdf';
---
<Base
  title="Resume | Dean Phillips"
  description="Dean Phillips: full-stack software development lead with 20 years of production software, bringing agentic AI into how teams ship."
  current="resume"
>
  <article class="wrap resume">
    <header class="head">
      <div>
        <h1>Dean E. Phillips</h1>
        <p class="tag">Full-stack development lead bringing agentic AI into how teams ship software</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="contact">
        <li>Oklahoma City, OK</li>
        <li data-phone hidden></li>
        <li><a href="mailto:me@deanphillips.dev">me@deanphillips.dev</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://deanphillips.dev/resume/">deanphillips.dev/resume</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/DeanPhillipsOKC">github.com/DeanPhillipsOKC</a></li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn screen-only" href={pdf} download>Download PDF</a>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>I'm a developer and team lead with 20 years of production software in .NET, Java, and Angular, across defense, payroll, mortgage, energy, and banking. I've led teams of three to 25 engineers, broken monoliths into microservices, and moved CI/CD pipelines to DevSecOps. Since 2025 I've been bringing agentic AI into delivery: first for development teams at work, and now through a multi-agent pipeline that builds, tests, and ships my own iPhone and Android app.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Skills</h2>
      <dl class="skills">
        <dt>AI and agentic</dt>
        <dd>Claude Code, Codex, multi-agent orchestration, MCP, custom skills and plugins, BMAD, LangChain, OpenAI API, GitHub Copilot, prompt engineering</dd>
        <dt>Languages</dt>
        <dd>C#, ASP.NET, .NET Core, Java, Spring, Python, TypeScript, JavaScript, Node, Angular, Vue, jQuery, HTML, CSS</dd>
        <dt>Architecture</dt>
        <dd>Microservices, REST, RabbitMQ, CQRS, Domain-Driven Design, Clean Architecture, microfrontends, Backend-for-Frontend</dd>
        <dt>Cloud and DevOps</dt>
        <dd>Azure, Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions, Docker, CI/CD, SonarQube, OWASP Dependency-Check, Trivy, Git, NPM</dd>
        <dt>Data and testing</dt>
        <dd>SQL, Dapper, NHibernate, Hibernate/JPA, unit and integration testing, Playwright, Cypress, BDD with Gherkin</dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Project</h2>
      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3>RepBunny <span>Independent, iPhone and Android app</span></h3>
          <p class="when">2026 - Present</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Shipped a mobile app with an AI-first workflow:</b> a strength training log for iPhone and Android (Vue 3, TypeScript, Capacitor) that keeps every user's data on their phone. It went from first commit to TestFlight in under three weeks, alongside a full-time job.</li>
          <li><b>Designed a multi-agent delivery pipeline on Claude Code:</b> an hourly GitHub Actions dispatcher starts cloud agent lanes that each take the highest-value issue from a scored backlog, build it, and open a pull request. An adversarial review agent merges it, sends it back, or asks me. Nothing merges without a full build and more than 600 end-to-end Playwright tests passing.</li>
          <li><b>Extended agents past the code:</b> monthly product, UX, accessibility, and security reviews that file scored issues; support email triage with replies I approve; App Store screenshots; and narrated sprint review videos.</li>
          <li><b>Automated releases:</b> signed iPhone builds go to TestFlight from the cloud with no Mac involved, and Android builds ship nightly. Its reusable Claude Code plugins are public on my GitHub.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Experience</h2>

      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3>Gateway First <span>Senior IT .NET Developer</span></h3>
          <p class="when">2026 - Present</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Modernizing legacy .NET applications and deploying them to the cloud.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3>Energy World Net <span>Software Development Lead</span></h3>
          <p class="when">2025 - 2026</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Pioneered agentic development at the company:</b> first lead to adopt agentic coding, building Claude Code and Codex skills and commands that captured the company's standards and ran automatically on related tasks. Put newly purchased licenses to work before the company had a plan for them, then packaged the customizations and demoed them so the other two development teams could adopt them. This sped up delivery and was a major reason the on-the-job training initiative shipped on time.</li>
          <li><b>Opened a new revenue opportunity with on-the-job training:</b> led development of an on-the-job training (OJT) module for the operator qualification platform that lets mentors review and sign off on OJT activities completed by their assigned mentees. Built at the request of larger clients, it opened a new revenue opportunity for the product.</li>
          <li><b>Led the team through BMAD adoption and expanded AI beyond engineering:</b> mentored the team on BMAD once the company standardized on it, helped extend AI-assisted workflows to the product and QA teams, and wrote BMAD architecture documents on the architect's behalf.</li>
          <li><b>Trusted with local architecture decisions:</b> led a team of three (two of them senior developers) and made architecture decisions within the team's scope, taking proposals that touched shared components or global APIs to the lead architect.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3>Heartland Payment Systems <span>Solutions Architect</span></h3>
          <p class="when">2022 - 2025</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Modernized front-end architecture:</b> led the conversion of a monolithic Angular UI into microfrontends aligned with team journeys, so teams depended on each other less and could deploy faster on their own.</li>
          <li><b>Moved from DevOps to DevSecOps:</b> added SonarQube, OWASP Dependency-Check, and Trivy to CI/CD pipelines. As security champion, helped teams fix what those tools found.</li>
          <li><b>Automated a multi-week manual process:</b> tax and compensation updates now run from Docker images hosted in Azure, which cut errors and kept updates on time.</li>
          <li><b>Stabilized the payroll system:</b> created and ran a technical backlog that raised Net Promoter Score by 31 points and cut major incidents from double digits to zero.</li>
          <li><b>Improved performance and integrations:</b> made an employee self-service app's pages up to 90% faster by moving its data access from WCF services to a Backend-for-Frontend with Dapper queries, and directed the FedEx integration's move from SOAP to REST.</li>
          <li><b>Protected sensitive data:</b> oversaw a key rotation policy and the re-encryption of large volumes of sensitive data with custom-built tools to stay compliant with industry standards.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3>Heartland Payment Systems <span>Senior Software Engineer</span></h3>
          <p class="when">2020 - 2022</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Worked across a large payroll codebase:</b> over a million lines in more than 100 repositories covering payroll, gross-to-net, tax, and compliance, keeping practices consistent across about a dozen Scrum teams.</li>
          <li><b>Shipped payroll features:</b> implemented the COVID CARES Act provisions, added multi-factor authentication with Azure AD B2C, and unified multiple user logins into a single email-based login.</li>
          <li><b>Improved architecture:</b> served on an architecture committee for a fragile, hard-to-change system, and introduced microservices for shipping and billing using Clean Architecture, CQRS, and Domain-Driven Design.</li>
          <li><b>Automated delivery and testing:</b> set up many YAML CI/CD pipelines in Azure DevOps, and worked with the tax and compliance team on BDD tests in Gherkin.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3>CoreLogic (formerly Mercury Network) <span>Senior Professional Software Engineer</span></h3>
          <p class="when">2018 - 2020</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Architected microservices:</b> refactored a large monolithic notification system into microservices with .NET Core and RabbitMQ, and delivered features and fixes for a public-facing ASP.NET application in two-week Scrum sprints.</li>
          <li><b>Built CI/CD for shared libraries:</b> a build-server-agnostic Cake pipeline for in-house NuGet packages, with semantic versioning from git history and stable and pre-release channels published to Nexus.</li>
          <li><b>Raised code quality:</b> added about 4,000 test cases across six legacy applications and services in the first year, bringing in NHibernate, Cypress, Moq, Karma, and Jasmine.</li>
          <li><b>Led a winning hackathon team:</b> led five engineers in a company-wide hackathon across three cities, building an automatic onboarding solution (two Angular apps and .NET Core APIs) in three days. Won 1st place for Best New Product or Feature, 2nd for Best Technical Solution, and 3rd for Biggest Impact.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>


    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Earlier experience</h2>
      <ul class="earlier">
        <li><b>Delaware Nation Industries, Tinker AFB, Senior Java Developer and Scrum Master (2016 - 2018).</b> Led the rewrite of 72 ABW SC's applications from Struts 1 to Spring Security, Spring Data JPA, Hibernate, and AngularJS, with two-factor authentication. Built an IDE-agnostic dev environment that cut onboarding time, and set up unit and integration testing.</li>
        <li><b>Sumaria Systems, then Delaware Nation Industries, Tinker AFB (2012 - 2015).</b> .NET Developer, promoted to Senior .NET Developer and Scrum Master. Moved Classic ASP applications to ASP.NET and jQuery, automated inventory reporting for logistics specialists, and kept production healthy with Foglight.</li>
        <li><b>Ensco Inc. (BAE Systems), Software Engineer (2005 - 2011).</b> Led test automation teams of up to 25 engineers across multiple sites for life-critical avionics software, and built their testing tools in C, Assembly, Ada, and JOVIAL under RTCA DO-178B.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="screen-only">
      <h2>What colleagues say</h2>
      <div class="recs">
        <figure>
          <blockquote>Dean has shown an exceptional command and knowledge of cutting-edge industry technology trends and architectural patterns. I'm in awe of his acumen and ability to break-down complex topics and apply them to sensitive payroll domain problem spaces. Furthermore, he has proven to be an excellent lead and mentor to younger engineers on his team.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>Maegan Womble</b>, Senior Software Engineer, Heartland Payment Systems. Worked together on payroll software, 2022.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <blockquote>As a leader, I found Dean to be honest and straightforward; giving clear direction and expectations. [...] He was able to resolve problems, give realistic estimations of time and scope. Many project leads within BAE sought him out to be part of their team.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>J Blake</b>, Principal Software Engineer, BAE Systems. Dean's lead at Ensco, later on Dean's team, 2011.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <blockquote>If you provide him a recommendation on a way to improve his code, he is open to considering that recommendation and sometimes comes up with an even better idea.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>Kristin Ferrier</b>, Founder, Ferrier Solutions. Senior colleague at CSI, 2013.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="recs-note">From my LinkedIn recommendations.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <div class="job-head">
        <h3>Broome Community College <span>Associate of Science in Computer Science, Phi Theta Kappa honor society</span></h3>
        <p class="when">2009</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .resume { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 860px; padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 32px; }
  .head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 8px 24px; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .head h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.2rem); margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .tag { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.08rem; margin: 0; max-width: 520px; }
  .contact { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; text-align: right; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .contact a { text-decoration: none; }
  .head .btn { grid-column: 1 / -1; justify-self: start; margin-top: 14px; }

  section { margin-top: 40px; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 0.8rem; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal); margin: 0 0 14px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  section > p { margin: 0; }

  .skills { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: 8px 20px; margin: 0; }
  .skills dt { font-weight: 600; }
  .skills dd { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }

  .job { margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .job-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; }
  .job-head h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .job-head h3 span { display: block; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0; margin-top: 2px; }
  .when { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .job ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .job li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .job li b { font-weight: 600; }
  .earlier { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .recs { display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .recs figure { margin: 0; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); border-radius: 14px; padding: 18px 20px; }
  .recs blockquote { margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .recs figcaption { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .recs figcaption b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .recs-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .earlier li { margin-bottom: 8px; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .contact { text-align: left; margin-top: 10px; }
    .skills { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2px; }
    .skills dd { margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .job-head { flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }
    .when { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  }

  /* The PDF. Plain black on white, letter size, no site chrome. */
  @media print {
    @page { size: letter; margin: 0.4in 0.55in; }
    :global(:root) { --text: #111; --muted: #444; --teal: #0b6e66; --line: #bbb; }
    :global(body) { background: #fff; font-size: 9.5pt; line-height: 1.34; }
    :global(.glow), :global(header.top), :global(footer.site), .screen-only { display: none !important; }
    .resume { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
    .head h1 { font-size: 22pt; margin-bottom: 2px; }
    .tag { font-size: 10.5pt; max-width: none; }
    .contact { font-size: 9pt; line-height: 1.4; }
    .contact a { color: var(--text); }
    section { margin-top: 12pt; }
    h2 { font-size: 8.5pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; padding-bottom: 3pt; }
    .skills { grid-template-columns: 1.15in 1fr; gap: 2pt 10pt; }
    .job { margin-bottom: 8pt; }
    .job-head { break-after: avoid-page; }
    .job li, .earlier li { break-inside: avoid-page; }
    .earlier li { margin-bottom: 3pt; }
    .job-head h3 { font-size: 10.5pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; }
    .job-head h3 span { display: inline; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0 0 0 6pt; }
    .when { font-size: 9pt; }
    .job li { margin-bottom: 2pt; }
  }
</style>
